# Gamebots in a trade window with a real player (Crafting 2.0 WP8, the full bot trade: BotTrades). New writing (see
# docs/bot-voices). Every gamebot can trade, so these lines are for every personality. The truth rule: a fact in a line
# is a slot the server fills from the bot's real state: {item} a real piece (its own for sale, or the slot it really
# needs), {price} the price it really asks, {count} how many pieces it really has for sale. The numbers of a trade (what
# is paid, what each piece is worth to it) are always said in the system window in the server's fixed words, never here:
# these lines are only what the bot says to you while you trade, as a player of 2003 would in /say or by /send.

@kind trade_reply
@who *
@levels 1-50

@topic trade_busy_fight
[in a fight|fighting], give me a [min|sec]
[busy|one sec], [got adds|mobs on me]. [after this|after the pull]
cant right now, [in combat|fighting]

@topic trade_busy_duty
on a raid [right now|atm], catch me after
[cant|not now], raid is forming up. [after|later] ok?

@topic trade_busy_trading
[one trade at a time|sec], finish yours first
[already trading|busy trading], hang on

@topic trade_timeout
[sorry|sry], gotta run. trade me again later
[gtg|have to go], [trade me later|catch me later]

@topic trade_come_closer
come closer and ill open a trade
[get closer|come over here], cant reach you from there

@topic trade_nothing_for_sale
nothing for sale [atm|right now], sorry
[got nothing|nothing] to sell [atm|right now]

@topic trade_for_sale
got {count} things, {item} for {price} and more. trade me and have a look
{count} pieces for sale, {item} is {price}. [open a trade|trade me] and see

@topic trade_wants_gap
always looking for a better {item}. trade me and show me
[could use|need] a {item} [actually|really], trade me and ill have a look

@topic trade_wants_maybe
maybe, put it in a trade and ill tell you what its worth to me
[depends|maybe], show me in a trade

@topic trade_done_swap
fair swap, [ty|thanks]
[good trade|nice], [ty|thanks]

@topic trade_done_bought
[ty|thanks], just what i needed
[sweet|nice], [ty|thanks]. been needing one

@topic trade_done_sold
[enjoy|wear it well], [ty|thanks]
[ty|thanks], [enjoy|pleasure]

@topic trade_done_job
there ya go
[done|all done], [enjoy|good as new]

@topic trade_job_failed
[sorry|bah], didnt take. no charge
[argh|no luck], you keep your coin

# A gamebot whose gear check found a gap posts a want-to-buy in /trade now and then (BotTrades.AdvertiseGap): {item} is
# the real piece it lacks (its armour type, the slot, its level), {budget} the most it would really pay (its purse share).
@kind trade
@who *
@levels 5-50
@needs wants_gear
wtb {item}, pst
[lf|wtb] {item}, paying up to {budget}
anyone selling {item}? [pst|send me a tell]
[need|looking for] {item}, [pst|send me a tell] if you have one
# Chat audit LOG-036 (2026-11-18): one wording twenty times in an evening; more ways to say the same true want.
[wtb|buying] {item}, up to {budget}
anyone have {item} for sale? [have|got] {budget}
[still looking for|still need] {item}, pst
{item} wanted, [paying|will pay] up to {budget}
[lf|wtb] {item}[, pst offers|, pst]
